// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6030 new: OpenAI Codex sandbox abuse detection rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6030
// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: OpenAI Codex Command Runner Execution by Unexpected User
// Sigma ID: d8f3a1b2-7c4e-4f5a-9b8c-1e2d3f4a5b6c
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Jonathan Johnson, Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-05-26 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, privilege-escalation, stealth, T1059, T1055
// Description: Detects execution of the OpenAI Codex command runner binary (codex-command-runner-*.exe) under a
//   user account other than the expected dedicated sandbox accounts (CodexSandboxOffline or
//   CodexSandboxOnline). Codex enforces its sandbox boundary by running the command runner
//   exclusively as one of these two restricted local accounts. Execution under any other user may
//   indicate a sandbox escape, token impersonation, or deliberate misuse of the command runner
//   outside its intended security context.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://jonny-johnson.medium.com/a-deep-dive-into-codex-windows-sandbox-a2489bf4ae91
//   - https://openai.com/index/building-codex-windows-sandbox/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/a20c16d6d3eef0c2c625df9d2ac3e18c1b12187c/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_codex_command_runner_unexpected_user.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath contains "\\codex-command-runner-" and (not((AccountName in~ ("CodexSandboxOffline", "CodexSandboxOnline"))))
